{
  "dom_id": "step-q152922",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}, & 0\\le x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{3}].$",
  "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the third raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{3}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{3}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}\\,{x}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(-\\frac{1}{x}){|}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}(1-0)+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(1-\\frac{1}{a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}+(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
